; Cloudflare Pages runs `npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1`, which re-resolves its
; own peers against the registry. Two of those peers now conflict with each other:
;
;   @cloudflare/next-on-pages  peerOptional @cloudflare/workers-types ^4
;   wrangler (latest 4.x)      peerOptional @cloudflare/workers-types ^5
;
; That is an upstream conflict we cannot fix from here, and it fails the deploy
; with ERESOLVE. Both sides are peerOptional and workers-types is types-only, so
; relaxing peer resolution has no runtime effect — the emitted _worker.js is
; identical. next-on-pages 1.13.16 also declares `next >=14.3.0` while this app
; is on 14.2.35; the build is verified working on that pair, and the pinned
; versions below keep it from drifting to an untested combination.
legacy-peer-deps=true
